ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: extra flag prefixes (comma-separated) for auto-detection, ON TOP OF the built-in
# defaults (flag, ctf, htb, picoctf). SET THIS THE MOMENT YOU LEARN THE REAL COMPETITION FLAG
# FORMAT ON THE DAY -- e.g. FLAG_PREFIXES=hackhaton makes the agent early-exit on HACKHATON{...}
# and find_flag_pattern report it. Without it, a custom-format flag is still shown in the model's
# final answer but won't trigger the early-exit/auto-capture path. Values are sanitized to word
# characters, so a stray symbol can't break the regex. The dashboard can also send this per-run
# (SolveRequest.flag_prefixes) without a server restart. Leave unset for standard formats.
# FLAG_PREFIXES=hackhaton

# Optional: allowed CORS origins for agent/api.py (comma-separated). Defaults to the Next.js dev
# port (http://localhost:3000 + 127.0.0.1:3000). Set this if the dashboard is served from any
# other origin on the day (a deployed URL, a different port, a teammate's LAN IP) -- otherwise the
# browser blocks its requests to the API. Leave unset for the standard local dev setup.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://192.168.1.50:3000

# Optional: per model-call timeout in seconds (default 60). Caps how long a single Gemini request
# may hang before failing -- the network tools already have their own timeouts, but the model call
# didn't, so a stalled request could otherwise freeze a whole /solve run (and the live demo). A
# fired timeout ends the run cleanly (think() catches it), it does not crash. Raise it only if
# legitimate calls are being cut off.
# MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60

# Required for the web_search tool (agent/tools/web_search.py) to actually work -- lets the
# agent look up a specific technique/writeup when search_vault and search_skills don't cover
# it. Sign up free at tavily.com (~1000 searches/month, no card needed) and paste the key here.
# Leaving this unset does NOT break anything else -- the tool just returns an "unavailable"
# message instead of crashing, so every existing eval/demo still passes without it. But
# web_search itself won't return real results until this is actually set.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Optional: comma-separated list of API keys for competition-day quota fallback
# (agent/model_router.py's _RotatingChatModel rotates to the next key on a
# 429/RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED error, and lets a key that recovers -- e.g. its ~60s free-tier RPM
# window clearing -- become the preferred choice again after ~90s). List order is priority
# order: put teammates' free Gemini keys first. Leave unset to keep using the single
# GOOGLE_API_KEY above unchanged.
# GOOGLE_API_KEYS=key-one,key-two,key-three

# Optional: paid last-resort overflow, used only once every key in GOOGLE_API_KEYS is
# exhausted. Deliberately routes to the SAME model (gemini-3.5-flash-lite) through
# OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible endpoint rather than switching to a different model --
# introducing an unvalidated model's tool-calling behavior as the emergency fallback is the
# worst moment to discover a quirk (see CLAUDE.md's Llama/gpt-oss-120b findings). Chosen over
# a plain Google Cloud paid billing key because OpenRouter is prepaid credits -- spend is
# hard-capped at whatever balance you load, unlike a GCP billing budget, which is alert-only
# by default and does not itself stop spending. Get a key + buy credits at openrouter.ai.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional: Full Telemetry (organizer's Next Steps slide, harness element #5/#9). LangChain
# and LangGraph read these env vars directly -- no code changes needed once set, every
# triage/think/act/observe/trim_context node and tool call gets traced automatically.
# Leaving these unset is the safe default: tracing is fully inert (evals/graph.py's
# __main__ suite behaves identically either way), and it's a real trade-off worth reading
# before turning on -- setting LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true sends challenge prompts and live
# tool output (including anything fetched from a real target) to LangSmith, a third-party
# hosted service. Sign up free at smith.langchain.com to get an API key.
# LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true
# LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=
# LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=ctf-hackathon-gambunta
